\subsection{The uber-polya Pipeline}

Each of the ten problems was solved autonomously by the \textbf{uber-polya} skill
of Claude Code Agent, following this three-phase pipeline:

\begin{description}
\item[Phase A: Model (uber-model)] The problem is received verbatim and formalized.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Phase 0: Problem reception and classification (Find vs.\ Prove).
  \item Phase 1: Identify the unknown, data, and conditions.
  \item Phase 2: Match to mathematical structures; propose candidate models.
  \item Phase 3: Build the complete formal model with mapping, constraints, and claim.
  \item Phase 4: Verify the model by specialization (trivial cases), symmetry, and completeness.
  \end{itemize}

\item[Phase B: Solve (uber-solve)] The formal model is solved with computational rigor.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Phase 0: Classify the computational/proof problem.
  \item Phase 1: Select algorithm, solver library, and verification method.
  \item Phase 2: Write a Python verification script (where applicable) with
    \texttt{Instance}, \texttt{Solution}, \texttt{solve()}, and \texttt{verify()} functions.
  \item Phase 3: Execute and verify. \textbf{If verification fails, loop back to
    Phase 2} (the iteration loop). This is the key mechanism ensuring correctness.
  \item Output: Solution Report with confidence rating.
  \end{itemize}

\item[Phase C: Interpret (uber-interpret)] The solution is translated for a general audience.
  \begin{itemize}
  \item Phase 0: Recover context (mapping, objective, audience).
  \item Phase 1: Reverse the mathematical mapping; state the bottom line in one sentence.
  \item Write a one-page layman explanation ($\sim$400 words, no mathematical notation).
  \end{itemize}
\end{description}

